# CLI follow-up

- `src/cli/provide.rs`: decide whether an invalid provided skill should be refused individually so the rest of the host bundle can install.
  Provided bundles are read strictly, so one invalid skill currently refuses the entire bundle; the host may then fall back to its own skills.

- Next minor after 0.41.0: remove the home-project window. `find_agents_root_from` then refuses a `--root` that is exactly home instead of opening it, and `warn_home_project` goes. Delete `--fallback-root` (`agents`, `skills`, `build launch-bundle`, `content::ContentRoots`' fallback layer) and its deprecation warning in `dispatch_result`.

- Next minor after 0.41.0: delete `mars provide`'s skill copy (design `mars-user-level` §3b). Hosts give their bundle to `mars sync --provided-root` (the host layer, `sync::layers`) and to lookups as `--provided-root`. Delete `src/cli/provide.rs` and its deprecation warning, `provided/reconcile.rs`, `provided/lock.rs` (`provided.lock` and its pending record), `ProvidedNames`' skill sets and `skill_outcomes` with its `Skipped` outcomes, `provided::recorded_skills` and the hidden set it feeds in `content::Claims`, the `.mars/provided/<host>/` staging read (`provided::staged_dependencies`, the staged digest in `ProvidedNames`), and the second-writer exception for `.mars/skills` (`sync::ownership`). A sync then removes the leftover copies `provided.lock` records.
